      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The typical stages of a CI/CD pipeline are indeed Code Commit, Automated Testing, Staging, and Production. At each stage, you can implement various gates and checks to ensure smooth progress and continuous delivery. Key checks and gates include: Code Commit - Initial merge checks, quality gate checks (e.g., syntax, linting, and formatting), and code approval from team members. Automated Testing - Integration testing, functional testing, or UI testing to verify component functionality. Staging - End-to-end testing, review by designated stakeholders, and A/B testing or canary releases to validate performance and user acceptance.",
